  nonce: '2647'  # 2647
  message: "WONT_DO 2026-09-09 -- THE PREMISE IS FALSE AND I FILED IT WITHOUT CHECKING THE SHIPPED CODE. Refuted the same day it was filed, by me, on the owner's instruction to tackle it.\n\nWHAT THIS ITEM CLAIMED: \"a `calls` edge is deduplicated by `(src, dst)` with the LINE discarded\", so collapsed call sites are unrecoverable and a consumer reading `line` \"has no way to know\" it is one arbitrary occurrence.\n\nWHAT THE CODE ACTUALLY DOES. `ir.deduplicate_edges` keys on `(src, dst, edge_type)` and **preserves every collapsed call site** in `meta[\"call_lines\"]` -- its own docstring says so in bold (\"The collapsed call sites are preserved, not discarded\"), and `_absorb_call_site` unions the lines AND every registry-declared per-call-site meta key (`per_call_site_keys()`), a discipline INV-vukiv already paid for. ABSENCE of the key is a documented contract meaning \"exactly one site, and it is `edge.line`\" -- which is precisely the \"way to know\" this item asserted did not exist.\n\nMEASURED ON THE VERY SURVEY THIS ITEM WAS FILED FROM (pretix, arm B):\n    18,075 of 76,635 `calls` edges carry meta[\"call_lines\"]\n    59,806 sites recorded, i.e. 41,731 sites BEYOND their survivors\nThe information I claimed was destroyed was sitting in the file I was reading.\n\nSO THE DEFECT WAS MINE. `diffsurvey.py` keyed on `edge.line` and never read `call_lines`. Re-derived through the documented field:\n    django.db.models CALL SITES   B 10,422 -> S 11,869   NEW 1,447   GONE 0\nagainst the +756 pairs / \"110 apparent removals\" measurement 0022 published. **The corrected result is nearly DOUBLE the published edge-level gain and has no removals to explain at all.** docs/measurements/0022, its README row and the CHANGELOG entry are corrected in the same PR; the retracted text is replaced, not struck through.\n\nTHE ONLY GENUINE BOUND is `_CALL_LINES_CAP = 50` (36 pretix edges reach it), which ir.py documents at the point it applies. That is a declared, bounded truncation, not a discarded field, and it does not resurrect this item.\n\nWHAT I SHOULD HAVE DONE: LIVE rule 1 -- the fix may already exist, GREP THE SHIPPED CODE AND THE TARGET FILE'S OWN HEADER before filing. The answer was in the docstring of the function I was theorising about. LIVE rule 2 is the companion and it names this exact failure: an item is usually right that something is broken and wrong about which part, INCLUDING an item I filed hours ago.\n\nRESIDUAL FILED SEPARATELY AND SCOPED CORRECTLY THIS TIME: an edge locates to a LINE, not a column, so two calls with the same callee NAME on one line are indistinguishable to a consumer joining an edge back to source. That is a different mechanism from dedup, it is what actually bit two of my instruments today, and conflating the two is how this item came to be filed wrong."  # 2647
